<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ngqika</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1778–<a href="/years/1829">1829</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ngqika was paramount chief of the Rharhabe Xhosa, grandson of Rharhabe, who struggled with his uncle and regent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndlambe">Ndlambe</a> for power. He sought British support, and after his defeat at Amalinde in 1818 the Cape intervened on his side, but in return he had to cede land between the Fish and Keiskamma rivers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ngqika.jpg" alt="Ngqika" width="320" height="280" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: I created the map, based partly on the source map: Eastern frontier of the Colony of the Cape of Good Hope from Algoa Bay to the … · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eastern_Frontier,_Cape_of_Good_Hope,_ca_1835.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
